FalcoAmadeus authors and attribution
=====================================

FalcoAmadeus is a fork of falco (https://github.com/smithlabcode/falco),
which is itself an emulation of FastQC. It is distributed under the same
GNU General Public License v3 as the original (see LICENSE).

Original authors (falco)
------------------------
Guilherme De Sena Brandine
Andrew D. Smith
Masaru Nakajima

All credit for the original falco design and implementation belongs to the
authors above. The original copyright notices are retained in the source
files.

FalcoAmadeus fork
-----------------
Joachim Wolff <wolff.joachim@mh-hannover.de> -- performance optimizations of
the read-parsing hot path and fork maintenance.

The fork keeps the analysis and report output identical to upstream falco
(apart from the "##FalcoAmadeus" identifier line in fastqc_data.txt and the
report footer). The optimizations were offered to upstream falco as a patch,
which the maintainers declined to merge.
